{
  "requirement": "Usage MUST record each provider request's outcome and available input/output\ntoken counts, including retries, with cached or reasoning-token counts when\nprovided. Missing measurements MUST be recorded as unavailable, not zero.\nRun totals MUST include request and tool-call counts by tool, elapsed time, and\navailable token usage, identifying incomplete totals without double counting\nprovider counters that overlap.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: false.** The behaviour is implemented and tested well, but one piece of implementing code lacks the required `{impl}` marker.\n\n**What is implemented**\n- **Per-request records.** `assess` (src/authoring/mod.rs) calls `begin_request` before every provider call and `end_request` after it, including after a timeout or error. Retries therefore each get their own entry. `RequestUsage` holds `outcome`, `elapsed_ms` and `tokens`, and the outcome is `completed`, `failed`, `unfinished` or `cancelled`.\n- **Token counts.** `TokenCounts` stores input, output, cached input, cache-creation input and reasoning as `Option<u64>`. `from_usage` copies the provider's `Option` values directly. A missing measurement stays `None`, which serialises as null, not zero. A failed request gets `TokenCounts::default()`, so its counts are unavailable.\n- **Run totals.** `UsageRecord` carries `request_count`, `tool_calls` (per tool), `tool_failures`, `tool_skipped`, `tool_call_count`, `elapsed_ms` and `tokens`. `tool` and `skipped_tool` count calls per tool. `tool_name` buckets unrecognised names as `unknown`, so model text is never recorded.\n- **Incomplete totals and overlap.** `TokenCounts::sum` and `sum_counter` keep measured subtotals and set `complete=false` when any request or optional counter is unmeasured. A run with no requests is also incomplete. Cached, cache-creation and reasoning counters are summed separately and never added to input or output, so overlapping counters are not double counted.\n- **Hidden retries.** Retries are not hidden inside one recorded request: `bedrock_sdk_loader` disables the AWS SDK retries, and the comment at the Ollama branch of `connect` notes that Rig adds none.\n\n**Tests**\n- **Token and request accounting (src/authoring/usage.rs).**\n  - `token_totals_keep_subsets_separate_and_missing_counters_unknown` covers subset counters, in-flight requests and failed requests.\n  - `partial_failure_retains_available_totals_and_optional_measurements` covers a mixed measured/unmeasured case, including a cached count of 0 versus a missing one.\n  - `cancelled_request_persists_elapsed_time_and_incomplete_totals` covers cancelled requests.\n  - `completed_requests_and_the_run_record_elapsed_time` covers elapsed time.\n  - `tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text` covers tool counts, failures and skips.\n- **Retries (src/authoring/mod.rs).** `throttled_requests_retry_unchanged_and_record_every_attempt` (8 failures and 1 success), `unanswered_requests_are_abandoned_and_retried` and `success_resets_backoff_and_retries_keep_history_without_repeating_tools` check that every attempt is recorded.\n- **End to end (tests/authoring_cli.rs, tests/authoring_batch.rs).** The Ollama test checks token totals of 22 and 14, `complete=true`, and the tool-call, failure and request counts. The Bedrock test checks the same fields for both the typed and untyped paths. The denied-read tests check the request outcome and counts.\n- Together these cover the main boundaries: missing versus zero, partial measurement, failed and cancelled requests, and retries.\n\n**Gap**\n- `bedrock_sdk_loader` (src/authoring/providers.rs, lines 151–183) is where `RetryConfig::disabled()` is applied. Its own comment says this keeps each provider attempt visible to the usage ledger. It is marked only for `rig_configuration_mapping`, `configuration_precedence`, `credentials` and `provider_backoff`, not `usage_requests`.\n- Only the thin wrapper `bedrock_sdk_config` carries the `usage_requests` impl marker. The test `bedrock_sdk_retries_are_disabled` is likewise marked only for `provider_backoff`.\n- Code that implements part of the requirement without an `{impl}` reference to it is a gap, and nothing in the source acknowledges this one with a FIXME.\n\nThe gap is narrow, but it is a real marking gap, so the judgment is false.",
